From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:49:08 +0900
Subject: Give java.lang.Enum its no-argument constructor whichever root loads
 it

An enum may write its parent as `java.lang.Enum[X]`, without the name and
ordinal that `CompleteJavaEnums` adds later. `Definitions` makes that typecheck
by replacing the loader of `java.lang.Enum` with one that, after reading the
class file, strips the parameters from its primary constructor and enters a
copy with both. But the class file is read for the class and its companion
together, by whichever is completed first, and only the class got the new
loader. A reference to a static member, such as `java.lang.Enum.valueOf`,
completes the companion first, the class is left with only its two-parameter
constructor, and an enum typed after it fails with "not enough arguments" from
source, or "wrong number of arguments" when it is read from TASTy after a unit
which uses the static member.

The module class now gets the new loader too, as a proxy, and the constructors
are adjusted in `doComplete`, which runs once for both roots.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: javaenumctor
---
 .../src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 tests/pos/javaenum-static-first.scala           |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/javaenum-static-first.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
index 007aa0445f56f71408446dc5f976e864f5117c6e..755bfbd22fa4924288a25fba636746b5ef04fc6e 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/core/Definitions.scala
@@ -786,11 +786,14 @@ class Definitions {
     // a new constructor symbol with 2 arguments, so that both
     // `X extends jl.Enum[X]` and `X extends jl.Enum[X](name, ordinal)`
     // pass typer and go through jl.Enum-specific checks in RefChecks.
+    // The class file is loaded for the class and its companion together, by whichever
+    // is completed first, so the module class must be given the new loader as well:
+    // a reference to a static member such as `jl.Enum.valueOf` completes it first.
     cls.infoOrCompleter match {
       case completer: ClassfileLoader =>
-        cls.info = new ClassfileLoader(completer.classfile) {
-          override def complete(root: SymDenotation)(using Context): Unit = {
-            super.complete(root)
+        val loader = new ClassfileLoader(completer.classfile) {
+          override def doComplete(root: SymDenotation)(using Context): Unit = {
+            super.doComplete(root)
             val constr = cls.primaryConstructor
             val noArgInfo = constr.info match {
               case info: PolyType =>
@@ -806,6 +809,14 @@ class Definitions {
             constr.termRef.recomputeDenot()
           }
         }
+        cls.info = loader
+        val moduleClass = cls.scalacLinkedClass
+        moduleClass.infoOrCompleter match
+          case moduleCompleter: SymbolLoader =>
+            moduleClass.info = loader.proxy
+              .withDecls(moduleCompleter.decls)
+              .withSourceModule(moduleCompleter.sourceModule)
+          case _ =>
         cls
     }
   }
diff --git a/tests/pos/javaenum-static-first.scala b/tests/pos/javaenum-static-first.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9321b8f13b08bcbdfafd81ba5c51e39f4b64f4e5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/javaenum-static-first.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+// A reference to a static member of java.lang.Enum, typed before an enum which
+// extends it, completed the class from its companion's loader; the class then kept
+// only its two-parameter constructor, and the enum's parent call lacked arguments.
+object Lookup:
+  def green: Color = java.lang.Enum.valueOf(classOf[Color], "Green")
+
+enum Color extends java.lang.Enum[Color]:
+  case Red, Green
